        "text": "If you want to create or mint your own nft, it's a straightforward process. There are various standards to do this. The Most prominent is ERC721, a standard for issuing and trading non fungible assets on the Ethereum blockchain. An Improved standard is ERC1155 on the Ethereum blockchain. It enables a single contract to contain both fungible and non fungible tokens, opening up a new range of possibilities. Ethereum has traditionally been the home of NFTs in their development. It has a large user base and well established NFT community, but transaction fees are very costly. There are a growing number of blockchain networks that you can use to mint NFTs, with some solving the problem of high transaction fees. On the Ethereum network.",
